      "sha256": "f6c8bd3da4537e132562e4f3370c1f3bd220edaf7e09ab696dcf865c931c1c47",
      "read_lines": "2061–2072",
      "operative_description": "The text says the 244–245 segment follows a canal that remains on Ukraine's territory and the 245–246 segment is a straight northeast leg."
    },
    "original_source_identity_context": {
      "path": "inventory/rus-ukr61-official-identity-followup.json",
      "source_hash": "4a5947e7497574d51f93255dfa7e03dce0c7acf6ecee52d25773a5205854a399",
      "relevant_records": "The 2017 represented UKR ADM1 OSM/Wambacher source identifies Sumy as an oblast; Ukraine Constitution Article 133, in the official Constitutional Court-hosted 2019 PDF, lists Sumy Oblast among the country's oblasts. The opened 2020 Rada summary concerns rayon reorganization under oblasts, not a demonstrated Sumy oblast boundary change."
    },
    "original_contract": {
      "path": "inventory/rus-original-contract-readback.json",
      "issue": 2302,
      "relevant_terms": "Keep the complete denominator and competitors, preserve source/vintage and source-role questions, do not claim current legal border certification, and complete every cell as supported, held, already-owned or explicitly unresolved."
    }
  },
  "independent_map_read": {
    "observed_labels": "On the retained page, the state-border heading names Ukraine and the Russian Federation. The margin labels Russia north/above the 244–247 line and Ukraine south/below it. The map is north-up; the Sumy key is located south/lower than the traced line under the conditional fit.",
    "vintage_and_scale": "N-36-128-B, 1:50,000, 2002 edition, terrain compilation 1980; map margin says coordinate system 1942.",
    "conditional_registration": "The assessment interprets the generic 1942 reference as Pulkovo 1942 / Gauss–Krüger zone 6 for the 33°30′–33°45′E sheet. It transforms the four printed geographic frame corners to candidate EPSG:28406 and transforms the retained native CRS84/WGS84-formula center with PyProj 3.7.2's best available EPSG:4326→EPSG:28406 operation. The fit is conditional: the map does not identify an exact datum realization; frame pixel picks are approximate and in-sample.",
    "distance_and_limits": "The existing trace assessment places the center about 0.55–0.60 km south of the 244–246 line across selected centerline and adjacent-stroke readings. It reports internal projected-grid darkness peaks with residuals up to about 15 pixels, but states these are not a confidence interval and may be other cartography. Thus this is a concrete adverse historical map observation, not a formal error bound, current-jurisdiction finding, or legal interpretation."
  },
  "source_specific_assessment": {
    "conclusion": "The evidence supports keeping this exact Sumy-contact key held and supports proposing a narrowly researched-unresolved disposition under the original outcome route. It does not support a positive RUS repair: the original target owner is RUS ADM2, while the retained source contact is Sumy Oblast and the treaty map places the key on its Ukraine-labeled side under the stated conditional fit. The treaty route text and map labels are specific to this corridor, so the conflict is substantive rather than an inference from a country-name or a missing modern certificate.",
    "reasonable_remaining_step": "No concrete already-identified accessible primary document in the retained record would resolve the historical center's placement more directly than this treaty map and route text. A separate independent geodetic validation could narrow the map-registration uncertainty, but the available residual figures are already materially smaller than the approximate 550–600 m offset and are disclosed as non-statistical; such validation is not a universal contract prerequisite and need not block a researched-unresolved proposal. Preserve the conditional fit and its limits in any proposal.",
    "scope_limits": [
      "Do not transfer this result to the other five Sumy contacts, the 51 Luhansk contacts, or the four Chernihiv contacts.",
      "Do not infer present-day sovereignty, operational control, or an owner change from the 2002 map.",
      "Do not delete the UKR competitor, source evidence, original key, native hold, or original package denominator.",
      "Root acceptance and accounting remain separate."
    ]
  },
  "actions_this_review": [
    "Read the revised trace assessment and its recorded source pins without repeating its trace or registration computation.",
    "Read the exact Treaty I-54132 text around route points 244–246 from the retained local text file.",
    "Visually inspected the retained N-36-128-B page image to confirm printed Ukraine/Russia map labels and route orientation.",
    "Read the original package contract readback and the retained official identity/vintage context."
  ],
  "disposition_effect": "Assessment only. No owner, native classification, selected cell, interval, or acceptance state was changed."
}
